ABCL HR Knowledge Partner
Architecture of the Unified Agent
The unified agent should orchestrate these 5 internal specialized HR agents:
Internal Agent	Purpose	Primary Users
HR Policy Agent	Policy interpretation and compliance guidance	HRBP, HR Operations
Onboarding Support Agent	New joiner onboarding guidance and documentation	HR Operations, Talent Acquisition
Benefits & Leave Agent	Benefits, insurance and leave policy support	HR Operations, Shared Services
Recruitment Knowledge Agent	Hiring process, JD and interview guidance	Talent Acquisition Team
Learning & Development Agent	Learning programs, certifications and development guidance	L&D Team, HRBP
The user interacts with ONE agent only.
Internally, the agent decides which capability to use.

Why These 5 Agents?
These 5 functions cover nearly 80–90% of day-to-day HR knowledge and support activities:
	1. Policy interpretation and employee query handling
	2. Onboarding support and documentation
	3. Leave and benefits guidance
	4. Recruitment and hiring support
	5. Learning and development assistance
This creates maximum HR value with minimum complexity.

Unified Agent Responsibilities
1. Interpret HR Policies
	• Answer policy-related questions
	• Explain eligibility and compliance requirements
	• Summarize policy documents
	• Identify relevant policy references
2. Support Onboarding
	• Provide onboarding checklists
	• Guide new joiner processes
	• Identify mandatory trainings
	• Provide joining documentation guidance
3. Advise on Leave & Benefits
	• Explain leave entitlements
	• Provide mediclaim and insurance guidance
	• Explain reimbursement policies
	• Clarify employee benefit eligibility
4. Support Recruitment
	• Retrieve job descriptions
	• Provide interview frameworks
	• Explain hiring processes
	• Support recruiter and hiring manager queries
5. Support Learning & Development
	• Recommend learning programs
	• Provide certification guidance
	• Identify learning paths by role
	• Support development planning discussions

Recommended Agent Flow
Example User Flow
Step 1
HR user submits a query or uploads HR-related documents.
Step 2
HR Policy Agent:
	• Identifies applicable policies
	• Retrieves relevant clauses
	• Summarizes policy guidance
Step 3
Onboarding / Benefits Agent:
	• Reviews onboarding requirements
	• Checks benefits and leave references
	• Provides employee guidance content
Step 4
Recruitment / Learning Agent:
	• Retrieves hiring guidance if applicable
	• Provides interview frameworks
	• Identifies relevant learning programs
	• Suggests development resources
Step 5
Final Output to User:
	• Policy guidance and references
	• Relevant onboarding requirements
	• Benefits and leave recommendations
	• Recruitment or learning insights
	• Suggested next actions and related documents
